README.md:117:Three routes can put the framework in front of Claude Code for a target repository, and they are **mutually exclusive per target repo**. The two supported routes (script and npx) write the same surfaces (`.claude/hooks/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.claude/settings.json`, and the install manifest at `.claude/.install-manifest.sha256`); the experimental plugin route instead ships a bundle with its own `hooks/hooks.json` under the plugin root and writes **no** target-repo settings or manifest — so manifest-based uninstall guidance does not apply to it:
