codex
- **P1 — Link allowlist still over-claims adopter symlinks.** When `_wbm_link_allowed` rejects a live symlink, control falls through to `-f`, which follows that symlink and emits a normal hash record. A skipped adopter symlink can therefore become framework-owned and later be removed by the manifest-driven uninstaller. The claimed confinement is incomplete. [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:352](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:352>), [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:360](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:360>), [scripts/uninstall.sh:217](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/uninstall.sh:217>)

- **P1 — Pre-v1.3 `--pin` produces false version provenance.** The marker record is dropped and the code claims the pin updated fallback `VERSION`, while this upgrade explicitly never writes target `VERSION`. After downgrading, both forensic reporting and the update checker can report the original/newer version instead of the content actually installed, breaking the advertised pin audit anchor. [scripts/upgrade.sh:1916](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1916>), [scripts/upgrade.sh:2131](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:2131>)

- **P2 — An install rerun can erase ownership of an emptied managed SPEC.** Continuity marks `SPEC/v1` delivered, but enumeration emits only files or symlinks; an empty directory emits no records, and the atomic rewrite replaces the prior manifest. The next upgrade consequently preserves the empty contract as unowned. [scripts/install.sh:2334](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/install.sh:2334>), [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:187](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:187>), [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:427](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:427>)

- **P2 — Protocol recognition violates dry-run write isolation.** The observer runs before the dry-run execution guard and creates its reconstruction tempfile directly under caller-controlled `TMPDIR`; if `TMPDIR` is inside the target, dry-run writes there. [scripts/upgrade.sh:1617](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/upgrade.sh:1617>), [scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:713](</private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.QWGyNu/wt/scripts/_framework_manifest_set.sh:713>)

Justification: Shell syntax, diff hygiene, AGENTS freshness, and contamination checks pass, but the two P1 findings violate the framework’s core ownership and auditability guarantees and make rc.2 unsafe to cut.

